{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>While he was still speaking with them.</b> Now according to the order of the verse, they are the ones speaking to him, and it should have said ״they were still speaking with him״ — for their answer came afterward. Or perhaps it is because the principal purpose of the narrative is to inform of what was transpiring concerning Jacob, therefore the verse hung the matter on its principal subject, which is Jacob." "<b>Or</b> the verse may intend to say that Rachel's arrival was while he was still speaking with them — she came before they had given him an answer. Only, the verse finished stating what they answered him in their response, and afterward informed of her arrival, and noted its timing — for it was at the time when he was speaking with them." "<b>With the flock that belonged to her father.</b> Meaning, all the flock that he had. This is testimony for Jacob, who said (Genesis 30:30): ״כִּי מְעַט אֲשֶׁר הָיָה לְךָ לְפָנַי״ and so forth — for a young daughter tends them." "<b>Or</b> it may say that the entire flock was sufficient for them by itself — <b>for she was a shepherdess</b>, meaning: expert in tending flock. And according to the first interpretation, its saying <b>for she was a shepherdess</b> means: even so, they were few, and without this they would have been consumed entirely." "<b>Or</b> it may say <b>for she was a shepherdess</b> — he divined his divinations and perceived that the flock would thrive under her tending, and without this he would not have demeaned his daughter, fair of form and fair of appearance, to tend sheep." "<b>Further</b>, it may intend along this line: <b>and Rachel came</b> — do not say that she was, heaven forbid, an immodest woman who goes out [in public]; rather, the reason is that she was their shepherdess, and therefore she went out with the flock."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:35.493606184Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}